## HI-04 — STILL LIVE; REVIEW PREMISE IS STALE (confirmed correction)
- `backfill.ts:109-145` — `idempotencyWhere` built per (table,column); NO guard exists.
- STALE-PREMISE CHECK: `apps/api/src/auth.ts:172` `ENCRYPTED_COLUMNS_MAP` is POPULATED
  (object literal with `account: {password,access_token,refresh_token,id_token}`,
  `session: {token,previous_token}`, `verification: {value}`) — NOT `{}`.
- CONCLUSION: the review's "while ENCRYPTED_COLUMNS_MAP is empty" framing is STALE.
  Phase 57 Track A populated the map; the lens encrypts those columns on write.
  The correct guard is a STATIC refuse-list of lens-managed (table,column) pairs,
  independent of any runtime map emptiness. The refuse-list must match BOTH the
  `session` model name AND the `sessions` SQL/backfill table name (table-name skew).
- Disposition: code fix — `LENS_MANAGED` refuse-list guard in `runBackfill`. RED→GREEN.
- CLI-default-map choice (recorded per plan): `DEFAULT_COLUMN_MAP` in
  `cli/backfill-encrypt-credentials.ts` was NARROWED to only
  `oauth_state.code_verifier` (the sole non-lens-managed column). Leaving the
  old 8-column default would have made the default CLI invocation fail loudly
  at the new guard; narrowing keeps the CLI usable for its one remaining
  legitimate target. The guard in `runBackfill` remains the non-negotiable
  chokepoint regardless of the CLI map. Two stale `backfill-cli.test.ts`
  assertions encoding the pre-HI-04 8-column shape were updated to match.

